hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2699","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb, narrated to us my uncle, who informed me on the authority of ‘Umar — and he is the son of al-Harith — on the authority of Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman, that a man from the people of Iraq said to him: “Ask ‘Urwah ibn al-Zubayr about a man who pronounces the talbiyah for Hajj.” So I asked him, and he said: “The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed Hajj, and ‘A’ishah (RA) informed me that the first thing he (ﷺ) did upon arriving in Makkah was to perform wudu’, then he circumambulated the House.” He then mentioned a hadith that included some details of the tawaf.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
